    "Find equations and intersections of straight-line graphs."
  ],
  "mastery_policy_key": "n6-default-v1",
  "sections": [
    {
      "stable_key": "n6-graphs-method",
      "position": 1,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Points, intercepts and intersections",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A point lies on a graph only if its coordinates satisfy the equation. The y-intercept occurs when x = 0, and the x-intercept occurs when y = 0. Two graphs intersect where they have the same x-value and the same y-value."
        },
        {
          "type": "display_math",
          "latex": "\\text{x-intercept: }y=0\\qquad \\text{y-intercept: }x=0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two accurate points determine a straight line. Choose convenient x-values, calculate their y-values, plot the points and join them with a straight line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "n6-graphs-example",
      "position": 2,
      "type": "worked_example",
      "title": "Find two graph intersections",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For y = -2x + 8, find both coordinate-axis intercepts."
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Set x = 0 for the y-intercept."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "y=-2(0)+8=8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Set y = 0 for the x-intercept."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "0=-2x+8\\Rightarrow x=4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "State the two plotted points."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "(0,8)\\text{ and }(4,0)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "verification_note": "Both points satisfy y = -2x + 8."
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "n6-graphs-recall",
      "position": 3,
      "type": "active_recall",
      "title": "Check your understanding",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Find the x-coordinate where y = 3x - 12 crosses the x-axis."
        }
      ],
      "response": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "comparison_mode": "exact_numeric",
        "canonical_answer": "4",
        "canonical_latex": "4",
        "accepted_answers": [],
        "absolute_tolerance": null,
        "rounding_precision": null,
        "unit": null
      },
      "feedback": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "At the x-axis y = 0, so 3x - 12 = 0 and x = 4."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "n6-lesson-04-summary",
